menu "ESP-Hosted frame copies (hosted_mem)"
    depends on ESP_HOSTED_HOST

    config HOSTED_MEM_FRAMES_IN_PSRAM
        bool "Keep esp_hosted's per-frame copies in PSRAM"
        depends on SPIRAM
        default y
        help
            esp_hosted 3.0.7 copies every received and every sent frame into a buffer from
            eh_host_port_dma_alloc(), which is internal DMA-capable SRAM. Up to 20 received
            frames (~33 KB) can be held at once, and when the allocation fails the frame is
            dropped without a log line. With this option those copies come from PSRAM; the
            SDIO transfers themselves are untouched. See components/hosted_mem/hosted_mem.c.

            Turning it off restores esp_hosted's own allocation exactly; the drop counters
            stay available either way.

endmenu
